WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:08.590
Someone tell me why there's a three second
teaser for the trailer, right before the trailer.

00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:11.800
I mean I already clicked on the video, I'm
clearly going to watch the trailer.

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:13.980
Why are you prolonging it?

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:16.380
Anyways, welcome back to Things You Missed.

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:18.820
This time I'll be looking at the Slenderman
trailer.

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:23.810
It seems like a lot of the suspense will come
from the question of what lies in the abyss?

00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:27.870
Is that just a group of skinny trees in the
distance, or is something staring back at

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:28.870
me?

00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:33.220
I wanted to analyse these images and find
out, but unfortunately, it seems that there's

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:36.170
only this one sighting as far as I can tell.

00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:40.030
It looks like the movie will be centered around
these three girls, which does make me wonder

00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:44.970
if they'll incorporate elements of the real
life Slenderman stabbing from 2014, which

00:00:44.970 --> 00:00:49.879
was a story about two mentally insane girls
who tried to kill their friend and claimed

00:00:49.879 --> 00:00:51.500
that Slenderman made them do it.

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:55.890
We also see this mobile thing, which contains
three girls a bunch of these other figures.

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:59.430
It doesn't look like they'll turn against
each other in this movie, but the idea of

00:00:59.430 --> 00:01:03.670
him getting in kids' heads and making them
do stuff seems to be supported by the dialogue:

00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:05.760
"He gets in your head, like a virus."

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:09.990
It would seem that this movie is based more
off of that news story than the traditional

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:11.240
creepypasta lore.

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:16.310
The original image from Something Awful forums,
which was the basis for Slenderman as a character

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:19.490
would have been a great easter egg to put
right here, but it looks like they're just

00:01:19.490 --> 00:01:21.630
taking it in a different direction with this
one.

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:26.390
The inclusion of these DeviantArt looking
ass Slenderman fangirl hentai drawings instead

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:30.830
is a clear indicator that this film is going
more towards a portrayal of the real world

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:34.510
effect of Slenderman's takeover, rather than
the lore-based one.

00:01:34.510 --> 00:01:38.280
Possibly a response to the critical failure
of the Marble Hornets movie.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:42.259
There also seems to be something about stabbing
out eyes in this movie.

00:01:42.259 --> 00:01:45.920
Slenderman has no face so he may be trying
to do the same to his victims.

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:50.530
We see multiple shots of eyes being stabbed
and several pictures on this wall include

00:01:50.530 --> 00:01:52.410
eyes and eye injuries.

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:56.759
This character's eyes are different colors,
aaaanndddd I hope you like black licorice.

00:01:56.759 --> 00:01:58.090
This looks like a shot out of The Happening..

00:01:58.090 --> 00:02:02.990
And when we finally see Slenderman, if you
slow it down, it looks like he could be made

00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:06.560
out of the same yarn material as those figures
on the mobile.

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:10.040
You also may or may not have caught this image
of Slenderman in front of a tree flash on

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:12.800
screen for a just a second at the end of the
trailer.

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:16.780
If you were unimpressed with this trailer,
let me know by giving this video a like.

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:21.060
I just wanted to talk about it because Slenderman
is an important part of what made YouTube

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:22.550
